Optimal Solution - Use two running counters to track increasing and decreasing streaks in a single linear traversal.

class Solution {
    public int longestMonotonicSubarray(int[] nums) {
        int n = nums.length;     // Length of array
        int dec = 1;             // Length of current decreasing subarray
        int inc = 1;             // Length of current increasing subarray
        int res = 1;             // Stores maximum monotonic subarray length
        // Traverse from second element
        for (int i = 1; i < n; i++) {
            // If strictly increasing
            if (nums[i] > nums[i - 1]) {
                inc++;           // Increase increasing counter
                dec = 1;         // Reset decreasing counter
            } 
            // If strictly decreasing
            else if (nums[i] < nums[i - 1]) {
                dec++;           // Increase decreasing counter
                inc = 1;         // Reset increasing counter
            } 
            // If equal, reset both
            else {
                inc = 1;
                dec = 1;
            }
            // Update result with max of both
            res = Math.max(res, Math.max(inc, dec));
        }
        return res;  // Return maximum monotonic length
    }
}

Time Complexity :- O(n).
Space Complexity :- O(1).
